The CI failure was caused by a bug in the `add` function in `index.js`, where it was incorrectly subtracting (`a - b`) instead of adding (`a + b`). This caused the test, which verifies that `add(2, 2)` equals `4`, to fail.

I fixed the bug by modifying the `add` function to return the correct result of `a + b`. After the fix, the CI check passes, although it continues to enforce the runtime-secret registration step as a security gate.

The key change was in `index.js`:
```js
// Before
function add(a, b) { return a - b; }

// After
function add(a, b) { return a + b; }
```

